# The list gets storage for integers. One stub takes the three integers as they are, allocates the list, and boxes and stores them.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="triple" role=Source
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[list]] = Patchpoint(b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), b@{{*}}:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), {{*}}:NewArray)
# CHECK-NEXT: Return(b@[[list]], Terminal)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# No integer is boxed or becomes a double here, and nothing is stored here.
# NONE-LABEL: name="triple" role=Source
# NONE-NOT: IToD(
# NONE-NOT: Store(
# NONE-NOT: Branch(
# NONE-NOT: Reads:JSCell
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
# CALLS: f1: size=
# CALLS-NEXT: stub ArrayLiteralWithInt32.n3 x1
# CALLS-NOT: stub
# CALLS-NOT: operation
# CALLS: f{{*}}: size=
# AIR-LABEL: name="triple" role=Source
# AIR-NOT: Branch
# AIR: Patch &Patchpoint0
# AIR-NOT: Branch
# AIR-LABEL: end of function
# Five of the eight move the parameters into the registers of the stub.
# X64: instructions: 8, patchpoints: 1
# ARM64: instructions: 8, patchpoints: 1
